From 2baed75f7deaa6e0fa41cad564e518cabeb9470a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Clement Lefebvre <clement.lefebvre@linuxmint.com>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 13:30:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] wayland: Implement wl_drm protocol to advertise render
 node to clients

Implement the wl_drm protocol and advertise the render node path on
client bind. This gives Mesa and Xwayland the render node path directly,
restoring hardware acceleration for both native Wayland EGL clients and
Xwayland Glamor.

This fixes acceleration for most apps and games in Wayland except
thoses which require dma-buf v4 (glmark2-es2-wayland for instance).

Note: dma-buf v4 (implemented in the next 3 commits) supersedes wl_drm
but wl_drm is a tiny protocol, costs nothing to keep, and potentially
covers older clients.

(cherry picked from commit 11d90f79fe866287b4aea0e96b9fc81ffc53ae6a)
